Practical 9 :-
Implement Hill Climbing for optimization problems

Prolog Code:-
 %f(X)=-X2+6X

value(1,5).
value(2,8).
value(3,9).
value(4,8).
value(5,5).

hill_climb(X,Best):-
    climb(X,Best).

climb(X,X):-
    \+ better(X,_).

climb(X,Best):-
    better(X,Y),
    climb(Y,Best).

better(X,Y):-
    value(X,V1),
    Y is X+1,
    value(Y,V2),
    V2 > V1.

% hill_climb(1,Best).

Output Query:-
1.) hill_climb(2, Best).
2.) hill_climb(4, Best).

Output:-
1.) Best = 3.
2.) Best = 4.
